---
name: __PROJECT_NAME__-development
description: Extend the __PROJECT_NAME__ Maximus project with routes, MCP tools, bindings and tests that follow its conventions.
---

Read CLAUDE.md and the Maximus skill (.agents/skills/maximus/SKILL.md) before changing the project.

- Add a route with `bunx maximus gen route <method> <path>`, then write its handler, its description and its
  strict input and output schemas. Its operation name, effect and scope derive from the method and path
  (`GET /v1/tasks/{taskId}` is `getTask`): declare one only where the derived one is wrong, and `mcp` or
  `rpc` only to expose the route there.
- Add a tool only agents use with `bunx maximus gen tool <name>`, in mcp/tools/.
- Write a handler as statements: name each result, test one condition at a time and return early. Move a
  loop, a calculation or a call to another service into a named function of src/.
- Put domain logic in modules of src/ named after their domain, imported as `#src/<module>.ts` from any
  folder, and what every handler needs in context.ts, scoped to `principal.organizationId`. A store answers
  what it found or `undefined`, and the route answers the failure.
- Name things in whole English words: functions start with a verb, booleans read as questions, quantities
  carry their unit. Give every exported declaration a one-sentence JSDoc.
- Answer expected failures with `fail(code)` from the catalog in errors.ts, declared in `failures`.
- Declare each binding in maximus()'s `env` with `bindings` from cf/config, and check what you read back
  from storage with `readSchema`.
- Cover each route in tests/ through `handler` from #maximus/http, its refusals included, with stand-ins
  for the bindings it uses.
- Run `bun run verify` before you finish. Never edit .maximus/; Cloudflare resources and migrations stay
  explicit.
